<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8567" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέφελος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unclouded, cloudless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴθήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.45
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					394a23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arat.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			, etc.: metaph., <i>not to be veiled</i> or <i>hidden,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1246
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνν.</span> is v.l.
				in
			<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				415
			</span></i>, etc.; <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				945.4
			</span></i> has also the form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεφής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
